# Template for dubplate-server's /etc/dubplate/server.env, rendered by
# scripts/deploy.sh from this file plus the sourced workstation age-store
# values (~/.local/secrets). internal/config is dubplate-server's own wall
# (config.go, keys.go); this file is its render manifest, not the wall
# itself.
#
# Three row states, so a later rung does not re-derive them
# (spec:1339-1348):
#   - A bare NAME= line resolves from the workstation age store at render
#     time, or deploy.sh aborts, listing every name it could not resolve.
#   - A NAME=value line is a literal: a value that will never be minted,
#     because it is not a secret.
#   - A commented-out NAME= line is a name whose value
#     arrives later, on the config.WallRow.Pending precedent: a row the
#     wall owns but does not require yet.
#
# Secret rows are bare rows. Two of them, DUBPLATE_MAGIC_LINK_SECRET and
# DUBPLATE_SESSION_SECRET, are minted through secret-set.sh and listed in
# ~/.dotfiles/secrets/registry.md before deploy.sh can render this file;
# until then the render aborts naming exactly those two. The five SMTP
# rows are bare as well, but the age store already holds all five under
# these exact names, so they need no minting. Every other row here is a
# literal: a value that is not a secret and is never minted. The
# DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT and DUBPLATE_SITE_NAME rows below are literals
# for a rename reason, not a secrecy one: the age store still carries
# the old names (DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_DIR to DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT,
# DUBPLATE_SERVE_SITE_NAME to DUBPLATE_SITE_NAME), and a bare row here
# would look them up under the new name and abort.

# Owned wall (config.go:216, keys.go's ownedWall): every row below is
# required by internal/config.Load with no default.

# DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT is the volume path that holds the music. It is a
# literal, not a bare row, because the age
# store carries the pre-rename name DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_DIR
# (internal/config/keys.go:165-166), and a bare DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT=
# row here would resolve against a name the store does not have.
DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT=/srv/music/library

# DUBPLATE_STATE_DIR is a literal, not a bare row: a path, not a secret,
# and the age store still carries an older value under this name, which
# a bare row would resolve to.
DUBPLATE_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/dubplate

# DUBPLATE_SITE_NAME is a literal for the same rename reason as
# DUBPLATE_LIBRARY_ROOT above: the age store carries the pre-rename name
# DUBPLATE_SERVE_SITE_NAME (internal/config/keys.go:165-166). Its value is
# copied verbatim from the store's DUBPLATE_SERVE_SITE_NAME (Resolution
# R7), never invented; see docs/HISTORY.md's Task 2 entry for the copy's
# provenance, not this comment.
DUBPLATE_SITE_NAME=907

# DUBPLATE_ADMIN_EMAIL is already minted under this exact name (no
# rename), so it stays a bare row: deploy.sh resolves it from the age
# store at render time.
DUBPLATE_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# DUBPLATE_IDENTITY_SOURCE is a literal, not a bare row: it selects
# which declared identity source is active, and "magic-link" is the
# shipped default, never a secret the age store mints.
DUBPLATE_IDENTITY_SOURCE=magic-link

# The magic-link source's nine required keys follow, then its two
# optional rotation keys.

# DUBPLATE_ROSTER_FILE is a literal: a path, not a secret. The roster
# lives under the state directory in its own directory so the unit's
# ReadWritePaths can grant it alone. The member verb creates the file;
# doctor reports it missing until then.
DUBPLATE_ROSTER_FILE=/var/lib/dubplate/roster/roster.json

# DUBPLATE_PUBLIC_URL is a literal: the server's public origin, which
# carries no path. It stays out of the age store because it
# is not a secret.
DUBPLATE_PUBLIC_URL=https://music.907.life

# DUBPLATE_MAGIC_LINK_SECRET and DUBPLATE_SESSION_SECRET are bare rows:
# secrets, resolved from the age store at render time. Neither is
# minted yet, so a render aborts naming both until secret-set.sh
# mints them.
DUBPLATE_MAGIC_LINK_SECRET=
DUBPLATE_SESSION_SECRET=

# The five SMTP rows are bare rows. The age store already holds all five
# under these exact names, so a bare row keeps a personal address and the
# password out of the repository.
DUBPLATE_SMTP_HOST=
DUBPLATE_SMTP_PORT=
DUBPLATE_SMTP_USER=
DUBPLATE_SMTP_PASSWORD=
DUBPLATE_SMTP_FROM=

# The two rotation rows are commented: optional keys, set only across a
# secret rotation so tokens and sessions signed under the old secret
# stay valid for the overlap. A bare row would abort the render while
# the age store holds no previous value.
# DUBPLATE_MAGIC_LINK_SECRET_PREVIOUS=
# DUBPLATE_SESSION_SECRET_PREVIOUS=

# Trusted proxy integration (keys.go's integrationClasses, "trusted
# proxy"): DUBPLATE_TRUSTED_PROXY_ENABLED=false is an explicit literal
# because running without a proxy is chosen, never fallen into. With
# the flag false, its two Required keys must stay unset (a row set
# beside a false flag is a load error), so they are not listed.
DUBPLATE_TRUSTED_PROXY_ENABLED=false
